What is in this directory, and what is not.

These files hold factual tables extracted from published documentation for the
units the archive measures: addresses, sizes, accepted ranges, initial values,
conversion values, and the labels the tables give their own rows. They are kept
so that what a document states can be held against what a unit was measured to
do.

The values in those tables are facts about the equipment. A fact is not
anyone's work, and they may be used freely -- in this repository, including the
models under `inferences/`, and by anyone who reads them here.

The documents themselves are the work of their publishers and are not
distributed here. No document file is committed to this repository, and the
prose printed around the tables is not copied: where a note matters, it is
restated in this project's own words. Each extracted table cites the printed
page it was read from, so a reader holding the document can check the
extraction against it.

The structuring and selection performed in extracting these tables -- the
schema, the page ledger, and the machine-readable form -- are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

This directory is deliberately outside `data/`, and the reason is what the
files are rather than who owns them. A row here is evidence that a page said
something; a record under `data/` is evidence of what a unit did. Kept apart, a
reader can always tell which of the two a figure is.
